WEBVTT

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:04.980
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:10.110
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:15.260
This is the story of their lives and adventures.

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:21.250
Riolu!
Use a flurry of Vacuum Waves!

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:24.110
Dodge them, Barrierd!

00:00:25.490 --> 00:00:28.290
Riolu! Force Palm!
Barrierd, you use Reflector!

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:33.010
Good, Riolu!

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:35.890
Let’s do this, Kamonegi!

00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:38.650
Super slow ball!

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:41.460
Not yet!

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:42.760
Draw it in!

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:49.680
All right!

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:51.230
Satoshi! Go!

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:54.160
Director Sakuragi!

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:55.860
I have a present for you two.

00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:57.850
A present?

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:03.500
Tickets to an official Pokémon World Championships
Master Class battle!

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:06.130
You mean one of Mr. Dande’s battles?!

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:07.880
Exactly!

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:09.880
All right!

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:13.310
I’ll catch more Galar Pokémon!

00:01:13.310 --> 00:01:14.930
Kamonegi, you come, too!

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:18.390
All right! Our destination is Galar...

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:20.470
Let’s go!

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:28.230
PocketMonsters

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:30.650
Hey, you still not ready? C'mon, hurry up!

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:33.230
You all packed and ready to leave?

00:01:33.230 --> 00:01:35.950
I'll show you this wide mysterious world

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:38.820
And skip the slow send-off

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:41.160
Be it through fire or through water

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:43.830
I'm fumbling blindly through the days

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:48.330
When I don't even know what the next second will bring

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:53.590
Each and every one of my memories

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:58.180
Can always be found inside a Ball

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:02.100
On 1, 2, 3, dive in!

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:07.850
I've got the future plans I imagined in my pocket

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:14.860
Greeting someone new is always fresh

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:19.070
No need (No need!) to hesitate! Try! (Try!)

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:20.410
Let's have a fight!

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:23.120
1: Once the battle's done

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:24.950
2: And we're laughing or crying

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:29.290
On 3, let's be friends!

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:35.960
Any day and every day, that's always been my rule

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:41.300
With this unpredictable, boundless world awaiting

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:43.800
Let's go! Every time you trip and fall

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:47.930
Let's go! You pick yourself up by my side

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:49.730
I choose you!

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:58.740
Dande's Ultimate Battle!!
A Heroic Legend!

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:01.570
Shoot Stadium, Galar Region
Ladies and gentlemen!

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:05.000
Welcome to the world’s
greatest Pokémon Battle!
Shoot Stadium, Galar Region

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:09.060
Oh, no! We’re late, and all because
you had seconds for lunch!

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:12.500
You had extra dessert,
remember?!

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:21.270
Satoshi, hurry!

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:22.810
Right!

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:29.030
Everyone’s so hyped up!

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:31.580
I ate a bit too much...

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:32.520
I know.

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:34.580
You wanna see the battle,
too, right?

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:35.520
Oh, right.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:43.160
The Championships have
over 10,000 participants.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:47.880
Among them, only the eight highest-ranked
can enter the Master Class!

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:53.770
To show our respect for these eight,
we refer to them as the Masters Eight!

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:56.680
Today is a battle
between these greats!

00:03:56.680 --> 00:04:00.240
It’s time for the battlers to enter!

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:10.540
The expert who charged his way into the Master Class
right after joining the Championships...

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:12.340
Current rank: 7th!

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:19.690
He is our very own Galar Region
Dragon Gym Leader, Contestant Kibana!

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:21.640
He looks crazy strong!

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:24.500
So that’s Mr. Dande’s opponent?

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:27.180
And who else would his opponent be?

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:31.700
Born and bred in Galar,
never having experienced a single defeat...

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:37.570
This ultimate trainer continues to extend
his flawless winning streak!

00:04:37.570 --> 00:04:41.840
Ranked 1st in the
Pokémon World Championships!

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:46.260
Galar’s very own superstar:
Contestant Dande!

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:54.610
You may use one Pokémon each!

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:59.210
The reason I signed up
for the Championships...

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:01.980
...was to put
your undefeated legend to an end!

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:03.230
I’m honored.

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:09.120
You should enjoy the tense, still air on the battlefield
and the cheering and yelling from the audience, too!

00:05:09.970 --> 00:05:14.860
No, this won’t be the kind of flashy match
that’ll get the audiences fired up.

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:17.380
They’ve got a severe battle
in store!

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:21.090
That’s great!
I’ll enjoy this to the fullest.

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:25.720
Both sides,
bring forth your Pokémon!

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:27.690
Go!

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:29.010
Go forth!

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:36.100
Contestant Kibana
sends out Duraludon!

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:40.730
And Contestant Dande sends out
his absolute ace, Lizardon!

00:05:42.050 --> 00:05:44.380
I knew he’d go with Lizardon!

00:05:44.380 --> 00:05:46.360
I’ve never seen that Pokémon before!

00:05:47.630 --> 00:05:51.650
Duraludon! Alloy Pokémon!
Steel/Dragon type!

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:57.460
Its body is made of metal so beautiful
it appears as if it had been expertly crafted and polished!

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:04.590
Let the match begin!

00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:07.040
Now, it’s champion time!

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:11.760
Bring the storm, my partner,
Duraludon!

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:13.150
Metal Claw!

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:19.510
No way?!

00:06:19.510 --> 00:06:23.570
Metal Claw rages forth, displaying a lightness
that defies its heavy appearance!

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:26.770
Lizardon, show them <i>your</i> claws, too!

00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:28.160
Dragon Claw!

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:32.810
Dragon Claw?!

00:06:32.810 --> 00:06:34.700
He’s changed up his moves
since last time!

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:35.710
Iron Defense!

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:39.970
It stopped it?!

00:06:39.970 --> 00:06:41.710
Talk about defense!

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:46.140
Another Metal Claw!

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:48.630
Dig!

00:06:56.470 --> 00:06:59.060
Duraludon takes damage!

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:02.700
Brick Break!

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:07.150
Duraludon,
counter with Stone Edge!

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:16.410
Duraludon counters with
a super effective Rock move!

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:18.390
Duraludon!

00:07:18.390 --> 00:07:21.420
Your strength does not disappoint.

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:24.080
I’ll wipe that calm smile
off your face!

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:26.920
Let’s finish this, Duraludon!
Steely Resolve!

00:07:33.170 --> 00:07:39.180
He unleashes the top-class Steel move,
Steely Resolve!

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:41.350
Steely Resolve?

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:42.900
What kind of move is that?

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:49.910
Steely Resolve is a move that sacrifices the user’s stamina
in exchange for immense destructive force!

00:07:56.170 --> 00:07:58.690
Lizardon! Flamethrower!

00:08:02.600 --> 00:08:05.210
The two moves clash!

00:08:07.060 --> 00:08:09.260
Steely Resolve hits its mark!

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:14.860
Oh, but...
Lizardon stands strong!

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:22.520
I thank you!
You have lit the fire in Lizardon’s soul!

00:08:23.260 --> 00:08:25.980
Then let’s make this
a <i>proper</i> show!

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:30.320
Let’s go, Duraludon!

00:08:30.830 --> 00:08:33.400
Kyodaimax!

00:08:38.590 --> 00:08:42.660
Kyodaimax Duraludon
makes its appearance!

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:44.170
Very good!

00:08:44.850 --> 00:08:49.630
I’m not finished with this battle.
And I won’t let anyone finish it for me!

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:56.860
I’ll show you what Lizardon
can really do!

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:02.140
It’s Kyodaimax time!

00:09:02.650 --> 00:09:05.150
It’s Kyodaimax Lizardon!

00:09:05.660 --> 00:09:07.050
Awesome!

00:09:07.050 --> 00:09:08.770
They’re both so cool!

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:16.320
Let the winds blow!
Stream forward, Sandstorm!

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:18.030
Let’s go! Dai Rock!

00:09:25.370 --> 00:09:27.340
Dai Knuckle!

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:42.720
Don’t give up!
Roar, dragon!

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:43.850
Dai Steel!

00:09:49.330 --> 00:09:52.770
I’ll show you a <i>true</i> champion time!

00:09:52.770 --> 00:09:53.990
Kyodai Hellfire!

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:08.370
Now, enjoy the climax!

00:10:26.170 --> 00:10:32.690
Duraludon is unable to battle!
As such, the winner is Contestant Dande!

00:10:38.120 --> 00:10:39.360
So strong!

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:41.820
Yeah... <i>Too</i> strong!

00:10:41.820 --> 00:10:44.120
You were great, Lizardon.

00:10:44.890 --> 00:10:47.780
We proved that we’re
the strongest once again.

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:56.550
Thank you for your support,
everyone!

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:00.650
Take a nice, long rest.

00:11:03.310 --> 00:11:04.860
My dream is...

00:11:04.860 --> 00:11:08.350
...to help make the trainers of the Galar Region
as strong as they can be.

00:11:09.430 --> 00:11:13.790
I expect great things from
the Dragon Gym you run, too.

00:11:15.780 --> 00:11:20.490
I guess me and the Gym guys should sharpen and polish
each other some more, and then I’ll challenge you again.

00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:27.200
I <i>will</i> be the one
to end your undefeated legend!

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:28.750
No, it’ll be me!

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:35.410
I’ll beat Mr. Dande and become
the strongest Pokémon Trainer!

00:11:35.920 --> 00:11:37.270
Hey... Even you, Pikachu?!

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:40.260
Satoshi...

00:11:40.890 --> 00:11:43.260
Of course!
I’m waiting for you!

00:11:49.430 --> 00:11:56.200
What’s this? Chairman Rose,
the one who raised Dande, is in the stadium!

00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:58.190
He watches with a wide smile!

00:11:58.190 --> 00:12:01.810
I see... So that’s Mr. Dande’s...

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:05.430
PocketMonsters

00:12:05.430 --> 00:12:07.320
Pocket Monsters!
PocketMonsters

00:12:07.320 --> 00:12:11.540
PocketMonsters

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:16.460
. Dragon .
. Steel .
Duraludon
PocketMonsters

00:12:17.970 --> 00:12:22.420
You think this is a statue of Mr. Dande?

00:12:22.940 --> 00:12:26.620
It kinda looks like his supreme pose,
but I’m not sure.

00:12:26.620 --> 00:12:28.570
It was something like this, yeah?

00:12:28.570 --> 00:12:30.790
No, no, like <i>this!</i>

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:31.320
Like this?

00:12:31.320 --> 00:12:34.790
You gotta look more heroic,
like Mr. Dande!

00:12:34.790 --> 00:12:38.070
Dande as the hero, huh...?

00:12:42.570 --> 00:12:47.320
Oh, don’t mind me.
I was just talking to myself.

00:12:47.320 --> 00:12:48.910
Um...

00:12:48.910 --> 00:12:51.580
Is this statue of Mr. Dande?

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:56.290
Oh, no! It’s of a legendary hero
famous throughout Galar.

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:57.560
Hero?

00:12:57.560 --> 00:12:58.090
Yup.

00:12:59.020 --> 00:13:03.770
Long ago... a great black storm
covered the Galar region.

00:13:03.770 --> 00:13:06.850
Giant Pokémon ran rampant...

00:13:06.850 --> 00:13:08.350
Giant Pokémon?

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:10.520
You mean Daimax?

00:13:10.520 --> 00:13:15.980
But they were defeated by
a single young hero bearing a sword and shield.

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:22.890
The statue here is meant to depict
the young hero of that legend.

00:13:22.890 --> 00:13:24.160
Really?

00:13:24.160 --> 00:13:25.520
A great black storm...

00:13:25.520 --> 00:13:28.170
Was it like a typhoon
or gigantic thunderclouds?

00:13:28.170 --> 00:13:31.000
We still don’t know what it was.

00:13:31.530 --> 00:13:34.950
Did the events of this legend
actually happen?

00:13:34.950 --> 00:13:38.910
Who was this hero,
and where did this sword and shield go?

00:13:38.910 --> 00:13:42.060
What sort of link
does it have to Daimax?

00:13:42.060 --> 00:13:45.250
Investigating all that stuff
is my homework.

00:13:45.250 --> 00:13:46.510
It’s, like, so heavy.

00:13:46.510 --> 00:13:49.130
Homework? For school?

00:13:49.130 --> 00:13:50.760
No, no!

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:54.020
It’s homework from my grandma,
who’s a Pokémon Professor.

00:13:54.020 --> 00:13:56.890
I’m her assistant...
technically.

00:13:56.890 --> 00:14:01.900
Um, I’m Satoshi.
This is my partner, Pikachu.

00:14:02.780 --> 00:14:05.440
It’s crazy cute!

00:14:06.150 --> 00:14:08.400
I-I’m Go.

00:14:08.400 --> 00:14:09.540
This is my partner—

00:14:10.150 --> 00:14:12.030
Oh my gosh!
This one’s super-cute, too!

00:14:12.030 --> 00:14:14.790
...Rabbifoot...

00:14:15.310 --> 00:14:17.720
We’re from Kanto.

00:14:17.720 --> 00:14:21.990
We study all kinds of things
about Pokémon as research fellows.

00:14:21.990 --> 00:14:22.920
I see!

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:26.300
I’m Sonia.
Nice to meet you!

00:14:27.640 --> 00:14:31.250
A black storm...
Giant Pokémon...

00:14:31.250 --> 00:14:33.680
And the legend of a hero...

00:14:34.360 --> 00:14:36.060
Sounds really cool!

00:14:36.950 --> 00:14:38.940
Hey, you two!

00:14:39.490 --> 00:14:41.570
Is there a Pokémon Center around?!

00:14:41.570 --> 00:14:42.730
It’s right over there.

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:44.290
T-Thank you!

00:14:44.290 --> 00:14:45.590
What happened?

00:14:46.790 --> 00:14:50.140
There’s this huge, weird thing
on the bridge just up ahead!

00:14:50.140 --> 00:14:51.080
Gah!

00:14:51.590 --> 00:14:53.290
Huge, weird thing?

00:14:53.880 --> 00:14:55.410
Let’s have a look!

00:14:56.680 --> 00:14:59.130
I don’t see anything...

00:14:59.130 --> 00:15:00.700
Yeah. Let’s go back.

00:15:00.700 --> 00:15:01.660
Sure.

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:15.420
Kamonegi?!

00:15:15.420 --> 00:15:19.980
But that thing it’s carrying
is ridiculously huge!

00:15:21.430 --> 00:15:25.110
Kamonegi! Spot-Billed Duck Pokémon!
Fighting type!

00:15:25.110 --> 00:15:30.990
It carries a leek more than twice as long
and heavy as itself with it at all times!

00:15:30.990 --> 00:15:33.510
It’s still a Kamonegi, though...

00:15:33.510 --> 00:15:36.590
That’s its Galarian regional form!

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:41.250
The same Pokémon can,
depending on its birthplace and habitat,

00:15:41.250 --> 00:15:43.860
exhibit slight differences
in its appearance!

00:15:43.860 --> 00:15:46.880
This is called a regional form!

00:15:51.350 --> 00:15:52.430
No, leave it to me!

00:15:52.950 --> 00:15:56.220
Now! Monster Ball, go!

00:15:59.350 --> 00:16:01.160
Guess I’ll battle it, then!

00:16:01.940 --> 00:16:02.770
Come out!

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:08.650
All right! A Kamonegi battle between
its Kantonian and Galarian forms!

00:16:11.150 --> 00:16:12.380
Crossroad Kill!

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:20.250
It used Crossroad Kill, too?!

00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:22.330
Not good...
Kamonegi, guard!

00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:30.160
Kamonegi!

00:16:31.240 --> 00:16:32.470
In one blow?!

00:16:33.520 --> 00:16:34.640
Return!

00:16:41.720 --> 00:16:45.190
So you’ve just been forcing
trainers crossing this bridge to battle you?

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:49.340
Fine! I’ll take you on!

00:16:54.500 --> 00:16:57.050
Riolu!
You came out on your own?

00:16:57.630 --> 00:16:59.750
I see. You wanna fight, huh?

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:04.460
Riolu! Vacuum Wave!

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:15.550
Another Crossroad Kill?!
Riolu, use Force Palm!

00:17:20.890 --> 00:17:21.900
Shadow Clones!

00:17:24.100 --> 00:17:25.770
When’d it get that?!

00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:28.900
It’s the results of our training!

00:17:28.900 --> 00:17:30.690
Follow it up with
a Vacuum Wave combo!

00:17:41.030 --> 00:17:43.790
Is it planning to fight us
with <i>just</i> Crossroad Kill?!

00:17:44.740 --> 00:17:46.790
Use Shadow Clones again!

00:18:01.720 --> 00:18:03.260
What?!

00:18:03.260 --> 00:18:04.580
Rotom, what’s that?

00:18:04.580 --> 00:18:06.140
It’s Brutal Swing!

00:18:10.650 --> 00:18:12.360
Riolu!

00:18:18.900 --> 00:18:22.170
Looks like it used up
all its strength on that move.

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:26.030
But Riolu looks to
be worn out, too.

00:18:26.030 --> 00:18:28.290
No. Riolu’s fine!

00:18:29.080 --> 00:18:31.390
I know you can still go on.

00:18:31.390 --> 00:18:32.420
Stand up!

00:18:38.050 --> 00:18:39.480
Come on, Riolu!

00:18:41.310 --> 00:18:43.210
That’s it! You can still stand!

00:18:43.210 --> 00:18:46.420
Come on, this is too much!

00:18:46.420 --> 00:18:48.100
I believe in you!

00:18:48.100 --> 00:18:49.850
Believe...?

00:18:49.850 --> 00:18:52.510
Riolu still hasn’t given up.

00:18:52.510 --> 00:18:54.780
So I’ll believe in Riolu!

00:18:59.770 --> 00:19:00.530
Riolu!

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:08.630
Satoshi, here it comes!

00:19:08.630 --> 00:19:09.930
I know.

00:19:09.930 --> 00:19:11.750
Time for the results of our training:
Part Two!

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:13.420
Riolu! Reversal!

00:19:22.800 --> 00:19:25.340
Awesome! That did it!

00:19:25.340 --> 00:19:27.680
No, not yet!

00:19:32.260 --> 00:19:33.930
Hang in there, Kamonegi!

00:19:34.640 --> 00:19:36.320
Stand up, Kamonegi!

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:39.200
Why are you cheering <i>Kamonegi</i> on?!

00:19:40.030 --> 00:19:42.450
It hasn’t given up yet, either!

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:45.450
Now, stand up!

